  "introHelp": "How to play",
  "intro1Title": "Goal: make words, pop them",
  "intro1Body": "Place the letter blocks from below onto the 8×8 grid. As soon as they spell a word, its letters pop and you score points. The game goes on as long as you keep room on the grid — aim for the highest score.",
  "intro2Title": "How are words read?",
  "intro2Body": "Letters are read only left to right and top to bottom, and a word needs at least 3 letters. A word across and a word down can share a letter.",
  "dictNoteTr": "The Turkish dictionary has base forms only, like KALEM, ARABA and GELMEK — inflected forms like EVLER or GELDİ don't count.",
  "dictNoteEn": "In the English dictionary, plurals and other inflected forms count too, like CATS and WALKED.",
  "intro3Title": "Points and multipliers",
  "intro3Body": "Each letter's points are shown in the corner of its tile. Longer words get a multiplier: 4 letters ×2, 5 letters ×3, 6 letters ×4… 8 letters ×6. Several words in one move make a combo, and making words move after move grows your streak multiplier. Clear the whole grid for +100.",
  "intro4Title": "When does the game end?",
  "intro4Body": "You always have 3 blocks in your hand, and blocks can't be rotated. If none of them fit on the grid, the game ends — so think ahead as you place them. If you get stuck, the Refresh, Joker and Hammer power-ups can help. A Daily Puzzle, the same for everyone, is also waiting for you every day.",

